# production.env.example — the deploy configuration, with placeholders.
#
#   cp production.env.example production.env    # then fill it in
#
# `production.env` is gitignored (see .gitignore). This file carries no secrets
# and is committed so the *shape* of a deploy is reviewable.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THIS FILE CANNOT BREAK LOCAL DEV, AND THAT IS BY CONSTRUCTION
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `agent/config.py` calls `load_dotenv(REPO_ROOT / ".env", override=False)` and
# nothing else. It loads exactly one filename, so a `production.env` sitting in
# the repo root is inert: no import reads it, and a local `uv run` behaves
# identically whether or not it exists.
#
# It only takes effect when something deliberately puts it in the environment:
#
#   set -a && . ./production.env && set +a && uv run uvicorn agent.api.app:app
#
# or via the platform's own env-var configuration, which is the better path —
# see "secrets" below. `override=False` also means a real environment variable
# always beats a file, so a platform-injected secret cannot be clobbered by a
# stale line here.
#
# **Do not rename this to `.env`.** That is the one action that would change
# local behaviour, and it would point a dev machine at mainnet with real keys.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHAT ACTUALLY DIFFERS FROM DEV
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 1. The chain is real ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dev runs anvil forked onto :8540. Production talks to Base itself.
#
# `DEPLOY_NETWORK` is load-bearing rather than cosmetic: Lane A derives the
# oracle staleness window from it, and anything it does not recognise counts as
# a real network, so a typo fails safe. On `base-fork` staleness checking is
# OFF (priceMaxAge = 0); on any real network it is 3600s. Deploying with this
# left as `base-fork` would ship a vault that accepts an arbitrarily stale
# price feed.
DEPLOY_NETWORK=base
CHAIN_ID=8453

# Must be archive-capable. The public https://mainnet.base.org is rate-limited
# and measured (#47) to crawl under write load — a plain `cast send` did not
# complete in five minutes against a fork of it. Use Alchemy/QuickNode/dRPC.
BASE_RPC_URL=https://base-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/REPLACE_ME

# In production these are the same endpoint. Several components read
# ANVIL_RPC_URL as "the chain to talk to"; pointing it at anvil in production
# would have the agent read one chain and write another.
ANVIL_RPC_URL=https://base-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/REPLACE_ME

# ── 2. Keys are real, funded, and NOT anvil ───────────────────────────────
# The deploy script *refuses* to run on a real network with an anvil account
# (`UnsafeAnvilKeyOnRealNetwork`), because those private keys are in Foundry's
# published docs and AGENT_ROLE can never be revoked — such a vault could only
# be abandoned. That guard is why these must be genuinely new keys.
#
# ⚠️ PREFER NOT TO PUT THESE IN A FILE AT ALL. See "secrets" below.
DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=
AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY=
# The agent key must hold AGENT_ROLE on the vault. The wrong key reads state
# perfectly and reverts every write on an AccessControl check, so it looks
# healthy right up until the first executeBatch (#11).

# ── 3. The API is live, and CORS is not localhost ─────────────────────────
# `fixture` answers every request and validates every response over invented
# data, so a production stack left in fixture mode looks completely healthy.
# Gate a deploy on GET /health reporting live on all three seams.
AGENT_MODE=live
AGENT_DATA_REGISTRY=curator_data:build_registry
AGENT_VENUE_REGISTRY=venues:get_venue

# Comma-separated, exact origins — scheme and port included. An origin not on
# this list gets a 400 on the CORS preflight, and the dApp then falls back to
# reading the chain and reports "the agent API is unreachable", which reads as
# a dead backend when the backend is fine. Include every hostname the site is
# actually served from.
AGENT_CORS_ORIGINS=https://REPLACE_ME.example

# ── 4. The model is hosted ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local Ollama is a dev convenience and a production liability: it needs a GPU
# or a very patient user, and the 3B could not reliably size a trade in the
# right direction. With XAI_API_KEY set the backend resolves to Grok
# automatically; without it, it falls back to Ollama and will try to reach
# localhost:11434, which in production is nothing at all.
XAI_API_KEY=
XAI_MODEL=grok-4.20-0309-non-reasoning
# ~$0.0015 and ~2.3s per decision at the steady-state cached rate. Leave the
# system prompt stable — churning it re-prices every tick at the uncached rate.

# ── 5. State must outlive the container ───────────────────────────────────
# Mandates, the decision journal, performance history and **open Aqua
# positions** all live here as files. Losing this directory is not cosmetic:
# a mandate cannot be recovered (only the hash is on chain), and an Aqua
# position cannot be recovered at all — Aqua can confirm a strategy hash you
# already hold but offers no way to enumerate a maker's positions, so a lost
# record is a position that can never be displayed or closed.
#
# Point this at a mounted volume, not the image filesystem.
AGENT_STATE_DIR=/var/lib/curator/state

# ── 6. Third-party credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────
UNISWAP_API_KEY=
# Per-process, not per-mandate. Set it to the ceiling the deployed mandates
# actually use: unset, the API applies its own 250 bps default and every plan
# is rejected in a way that reads as "the agent will not trade".
UNISWAP_SLIPPAGE_BPS=50
GRAPH_API_KEY=
TOKEN_API_KEY=
BASESCAN_API_KEY=

# ── 7. The browser build ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* are inlined at BUILD time, not read at runtime. Changing them
# needs a rebuild — setting them only in the runtime environment silently
# leaves the previous values compiled into the bundle.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.REPLACE_ME.example
NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID=8453
NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_ID=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRETS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Prefer the platform's secret store and leave every value above blank here.
# A file on disk is the failure mode this repo has already had: `env.txt` was
# committed via `git add -A` with eight live credentials, and the remediation
# was rotation, not a history rewrite — once a blob is pushed it stays
# fetchable by its SHA. `.gitignore` now matches this filename explicitly, but
# a value that is never written to a file cannot be committed by any command.
#
# Rotation order and the current exposure are in docs/secrets.md.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PRE-DEPLOY CHECKS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   1. GET /health              -> "mode":"live" on all three seams
#   2. GET /venues              -> the venues you expect, not a 503
#   3. A CORS preflight from the real origin returns 200, not 400:
#        curl -X OPTIONS $API/health -H "Origin: https://your.site" \
#             -H "Access-Control-Request-Method: GET" -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n'
#   4. AGENT_STATE_DIR is a mounted volume and survives a restart
#   5. The agent address matches the vault's `agent` in GET /vault/{addr}/state
